    {
      "lang": "zh",
      "label": "树的序列化：用空标记记录结构",
      "href": "../297/#step1",
      "observed": "0202 逐 token 解码解码从串的左端开始。读到数字就创建节点；读到 # 就返回空子树。创建数字后，必须先完整读完左子树，再读右子树。cursor 是下一个未读 token 的下标。每一步只消费一个 token，账本显示“读前 → 读后”。示例树[1,2,3,null,null,4,5]只有根 [8]空树 []左链 [1,2,null,null]负值 [-1,0,2]自定义串应用 token 串上一步下一 token重置已消费 0/11 个 token按“下一 token”观察每个 token 如何落到树上。Token 串12##34##5##当前递归结果∅递归账本"
    },
    {
      "lang": "zh",
      "label": "竖直遍历：用坐标描述树中位置",
      "href": "../987/#step1",
      "observed": "1 · 三个节点落在哪一列？给定二叉树（每个节点最多有左、右两个孩子），求按列排列的节点值列表。以根节点 8 为起点：行 row 是向下走的边数，列 col 是向右一步加 1、向左一步减 1 的总和。根是 (0,0)，左孩子 4 是 (1,−1)，右孩子 6 是 (1,1)。    8 (0,0)\n   / \\\n  4   6\n(1,−1) (1,1)列 −1 → [4]；列 0 → [8]；列 1 → [6]。从最左列读起，得到 [[4],[8],[6]]。列里存的是值，不是坐标，也不补空位。官方范围：1–1000 个节点，节点值 0–1000。每列先按行从小到大；只有同一行、同一列的节点才按值从小到大。重复值必须保留。"
    },
    {
      "lang": "en",
      "label": "Tree serialization: encode structure with null markers",
      "href": "../297/#step1",
      "observed": "0202 Decode one tokenDecoding starts at the left edge. A number creates a node; # returns an empty subtree. After a number, consume the complete left subtree before the right subtree.The cursor is the index of the next unread token. Each step consumes one token; the ledger shows before → after.Tree preset[1,2,3,null,null,4,5]Root only [8]Empty []Left chain [1,2,null,null]Negative values [-1,0,2]Custom stringApply tokensPreviousNext tokenResetConsumed 0/11 tokensPress “Next token” to see where each token lands.Token string12##34##5##Current recursive result∅Recursive ledger"
    },
    {
      "lang": "en",
      "label": "Vertical traversal: describe tree positions with coordinates",
      "href": "../987/#step1",
      "observed": "1 · Which column holds each of three nodes?Given a binary tree (each node has at most a left and a right child), return lists of node values grouped by column. Start at root 8: row counts edges downward; col adds 1 for each right edge and subtracts 1 for each left edge. The root is (0,0), its left child 4 is (1,−1), and its right child 6 is (1,1).    8 (0,0)\n   / \\\n  4   6\n(1,−1) (1,1)Column −1 → [4]; column 0 → [8]; column 1 → [6]. Read from the leftmost column: [[4],[8],[6]]. Lists contain values, not coordinates, and contain no empty placeholders.Official bounds: 1–1000 nodes, values 0–1000. Within each column, rows increase first; only nodes sharing both row and column are ordered by value. Keep repeated values."
    }
